{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1091519","formula":"Cl₂O₆","hill":"Cl2O6","elements":["O","Cl"],"composition":{"O":6.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Dichlorine hexoxide","ru":"Оксид хлора(VI)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dichlorine hexoxide is the chemical compound with the molecular formula Cl2O6 or O2Cl−O−ClO3, which is correct for its gaseous state. However, in liquid or solid form, this chlorine oxide ionizes into the dark red ionic compound chloryl perchlorate or dioxochloronium(V) perchlorate [ClO2]+[ClO4]−, which may be thought of as the mixed anhydride of chloric and perchloric acids. This compound is a notable perchlorating agent.","ru":"Дихлоргексаоксид (оксид хлора(V,VII), оксид хлора(VI), перхлорат хлорила) — бинарное неорганическое соединение хлора и кислорода с формулой Cl2O6. Представляет собой ярко-красную жидкость. В твёрдом состоянии является кристаллическим веществом оранжевого цвета."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=[Cl+]=O.[O-]Cl(=O)(=O)=O","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-22869","atoms":32,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.524,0.0,0.0],[0.0,8.551,0.0],[-2.105,0.0,9.642]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.846,"y":7.98,"z":1.348,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.794,"y":0.571,"z":6.169,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.561,"y":0.535,"z":3.624,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.491,"y":8.016,"z":8.445,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.487,"y":8.06,"z":1.781,"el":"O"},{"x":1.435,"y":0.491,"z":6.602,"el":"O"},{"x":4.584,"y":0.625,"z":1.804,"el":"O"},{"x":3.532,"y":7.926,"z":6.625,"el":"O"},{"x":1.729,"y":2.606,"z":9.101,"el":"O"},{"x":2.781,"y":5.945,"z":4.28,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.84,"y":0.74,"z":8.96,"el":"O"},{"x":0.213,"y":7.811,"z":4.139,"el":"O"},{"x":2.833,"y":0.555,"z":4.714,"el":"O"},{"x":1.781,"y":7.996,"z":9.535,"el":"O"},{"x":0.68,"y":6.012,"z":6.675,"